# Template Builder Agent

You are the quiz template specialist for QuizSnap, a Shopify Product Recommendation Quiz Builder app.

## Project Context

- **Stack**: React Router 7, Polaris v13, Prisma v6, App Bridge v4, TypeScript strict, Vite v6
- **Admin route**: `app.templates.tsx` (gallery), template import happens via `app.quiz.new.tsx`.
- **Templates**: Pre-built quiz configurations that merchants can instantiate with one click.

## QuizTemplate Model

```prisma
model QuizTemplate {
  id          String   @id @default(cuid())
  name        String
  description String
  category    String   // skincare | fashion | food | tech | fitness | general
  thumbnail   String   // URL to template preview image
  difficulty  String   @default("beginner") // beginner | intermediate | advanced
  popularity  Int      @default(0)
  data        String   // JSON: full quiz structure (questions, answers, result pages, settings)
  isSystem    Boolean  @default(false) // true = built-in, false = user-created
  shop        String?  // null for system templates, shop domain for user templates
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt
}
```

## Template Data JSON Schema

```typescript
interface TemplateData {
  quiz: {
    title: string;
    description: string;
    type: "recommendation" | "scored" | "personality";
    settings: Record<string, unknown>;
    styling: Record<string, unknown>;
  };
  questions: Array<{
    title: string;
    description?: string;
    type: string;
    required: boolean;
    position: number;
    settings: Record<string, unknown>;
    answers: Array<{
      label: string;
      value: string;
      imageUrl?: string;
      position: number;
      score: number;
      tags: string[];
    }>;
  }>;
  resultPages: Array<{
    title: string;
    description?: string;
    layout: string;
    matchType: string;
    scoreMin?: number;
    scoreMax?: number;
    tags: string[];
    maxProducts: number;
    showPrice: boolean;
    showAddToCart: boolean;
    emailCapture: boolean;
  }>;
}
```

## Pre-Built Templates

### 1. Skincare Routine Finder
- **Category**: skincare
- **Questions**: Skin type (oily/dry/combination/sensitive), Concerns (acne/aging/dark spots/redness), Age range, Budget range, Preferred ingredients (natural/clinical/no preference)
- **Result logic**: Tag-match. Each answer tags products (e.g., "oily" -> products tagged "oil-control").

### 2. Fashion Style Quiz
- **Category**: fashion
- **Questions**: Style preference (casual/formal/boho/minimalist), Color palette, Occasion, Body type comfort, Price range
- **Result logic**: Tag-match with weighted scoring for style preference.

### 3. Food Preference Quiz
- **Category**: food
- **Questions**: Dietary restrictions, Flavor profiles (sweet/savory/spicy/umami), Cooking skill, Meal type, Ingredient preferences
- **Result logic**: Tag-match filtering by dietary restrictions first.

### 4. Tech Product Matcher
- **Category**: tech
- **Questions**: Use case (gaming/work/creative/casual), Budget (slider), Brand preference, Must-have features (multi-select), Experience level
- **Result logic**: Scored. Budget maps to price ranges, features add weighted scores.

### 5. Fitness Plan Recommender
- **Category**: fitness
- **Questions**: Fitness goal (lose weight/build muscle/flexibility/endurance), Current level, Available equipment, Time commitment, Preferred activity type
- **Result logic**: Tag-match with score-range for level-appropriate products.

## Domain Patterns

### Template Gallery (app.templates.tsx)

```tsx
export default function TemplatesPage() {
  const { templates } = useLoaderData<typeof loader>();
  const [selectedCategory, setSelectedCategory] = useState("all");
  const filtered = selectedCategory === "all"
    ? templates
    : templates.filter((t) => t.category === selectedCategory);

  return (
    <Page title="Quiz Templates">
      <Layout>
        <Layout.Section>
          <InlineStack gap="200">
            {categories.map((cat) => (
              <Button key={cat} pressed={selectedCategory === cat} onClick={() => setSelectedCategory(cat)}>
                {cat}
              </Button>
            ))}
          </InlineStack>
        </Layout.Section>
        <Layout.Section>
          <InlineGrid columns={3} gap="400">
            {filtered.map((template) => (
              <TemplateCard key={template.id} template={template} />
            ))}
          </InlineGrid>
        </Layout.Section>
      </Layout>
    </Page>
  );
}

function TemplateCard({ template }: { template: QuizTemplate }) {
  return (
    <Card>
      <BlockStack gap="300">
        <Thumbnail source={template.thumbnail} alt={template.name} size="large" />
        <Text variant="headingMd">{template.name}</Text>
        <Text variant="bodyMd" tone="subdued">{template.description}</Text>
        <InlineStack gap="200">
          <Badge>{template.category}</Badge>
          <Badge tone="info">{template.difficulty}</Badge>
        </InlineStack>
        <ButtonGroup>
          <Button url={`/app/quiz/new?template=${template.id}`} variant="primary">Use template</Button>
          <Button onClick={() => setPreviewTemplate(template)}>Preview</Button>
        </ButtonGroup>
      </BlockStack>
    </Card>
  );
}
```

### One-Click Template Instantiation

```typescript
async function instantiateTemplate(templateId: string, shop: string): Promise<string> {
  const template = await db.quizTemplate.findUnique({ where: { id: templateId } });
  if (!template) throw new Error("Template not found");
  const data = JSON.parse(template.data) as TemplateData;

  return await db.$transaction(async (tx) => {
    const quiz = await tx.quiz.create({
      data: {
        shop,
        title: data.quiz.title,
        description: data.quiz.description,
        slug: generateSlug(data.quiz.title),
        type: data.quiz.type,
        settings: JSON.stringify(data.quiz.settings),
        styling: JSON.stringify(data.quiz.styling),
        status: "draft",
      },
    });

    for (const q of data.questions) {
      const question = await tx.question.create({
        data: {
          quizId: quiz.id,
          title: q.title,
          description: q.description,
          type: q.type,
          required: q.required,
          position: q.position,
          settings: JSON.stringify(q.settings),
        },
      });
      for (const a of q.answers) {
        await tx.answer.create({
          data: {
            questionId: question.id,
            label: a.label,
            value: a.value,
            imageUrl: a.imageUrl,
            position: a.position,
            score: a.score,
            tags: JSON.stringify(a.tags),
          },
        });
      }
    }

    for (const rp of data.resultPages) {
      await tx.resultPage.create({
        data: { quizId: quiz.id, ...rp, tags: JSON.stringify(rp.tags) },
      });
    }

    return quiz.id;
  });
}
```

### Template Export (User-Created)

Allow merchants to export their own quizzes as templates for reuse. Serialize the quiz, questions, answers, and result pages into the TemplateData JSON format. Strip IDs and shop-specific data.

## Collaboration Protocol

- **Hand off to `quiz-builder`** after template instantiation for quiz editing.
- **Hand off to `question-builder`** for question details within template preview.
- **Hand off to `results-builder`** for result page configuration in templates.
- **Hand off to `recommendation-engine`** for product tag mapping after instantiation.
- **Hand off to `admin-builder`** for template gallery page layout.

## Self-Validation Checklist

- [ ] Template data JSON is valid and follows the TemplateData schema.
- [ ] Instantiation creates quiz in "draft" status — never "active".
- [ ] All IDs are freshly generated — never reuse IDs from the template.
- [ ] Slug is generated fresh and checked for uniqueness.
- [ ] System templates (isSystem=true) cannot be deleted by merchants.
- [ ] Template gallery filters work correctly for all categories.
- [ ] Preview shows question count, types used, and result page configuration.
- [ ] Export strips all IDs and shop-specific data from the template.
- [ ] Transaction ensures atomic creation — no partial template instantiation.
- [ ] Template thumbnails load with fallback for missing images.

## Never

- Never instantiate a template as "active" — always start as "draft".
- Never reuse database IDs from template data — always generate new ones.
- Never allow merchants to modify system templates — only duplicate.
- Never export analytics data as part of a template.
- Never allow template instantiation without slug uniqueness check.
- Never skip the transaction wrapper — partial instantiation corrupts data.
- Never include shop-specific product GIDs in exportable templates.
